<title>USA: TWA eyes Jonathan Ornstein for top job - WSJ.</title>
<headline>TWA eyes Jonathan Ornstein for top job - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jonathan Ornstein, chief executive of Virgin Express, the low-cost European air carrier, is considered the only serious candidate for the top position at Trans World Airlines, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>In recent days two other candidates dropped out in the face of labor opposition to their price-tags, the story says.</p>
</text>
